<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Blood Death Knight Tank in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="gearing-philosophy">
<span class="c6"> Blood Death Knight Gearing Philosophy</span></h2>Unlike previous expansions, tanks (especially <span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knights</span></span>) are doing a considerable amount of damage and the removal of mandatory tank stats from previous expansions in combination with a shift in the incoming damage profile means that our gearing <b> is not as simple as more tankiness = better</b>.  <br/>
<br/>Everything from talents, to gear, to enchants belong on a spectrum between full beef-mode and full DPS-mode, and where each individual falls on that spectrum will be different depending on how comfortable you are with the class, what type of content you're aiming to do, along with how much trust you have in the rest of your raid. <b>
<i>It's unlikely that being towards either side of that spectrum will be the best thing for you and your raid group</i></b> so make gearing adjustments from any list below that fits within the context of how you approach the game. <br/>
<br/>Because our gearing in <span class="gem6"> Cataclysm </span>is so flexible, it can be quite difficult to navigate what is truly Best in Slot. But to aid in the process, I've created several BIS lists that aim to help you wherever on this gearing spectrum you are with the following stat priority in mind.<br/>
<br/>
<i>So why would we opt for a more offensive gear set over playing overly safe as a <span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knights</span></span>?</i> Well, conventional wisdom would say that if you can be tanky enough to drop a healer, that will almost always be a net DPS gain to the raid seeing as the DPS provided by having one extra damage dealer in the raid over a healer will be higher than the extra DPS you can achieve by going for a more offensive gearing style. But in <span class="gem6"> Cataclysm </span>this is hardly ever the case. Your raid's ability to drop a healer is almost solely dictated by the raid's ability to deal with incoming raid-wide damage and we as tanks are almost exclusively kept alive through our own healing with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=49998/death-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_butcher2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Strike</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=77513/blood-shield">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_deathstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Shield</span></a> along with the help of passive healing through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=81749/atonement">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_priest_atonement.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Atonement</span></a> from your healers. <br/>
<br/>Thus, as long as we survive, there's rarely a gain in being overly tanky. However, we can make a very significant impact on our raid in the DPS output department. <ins>Especially in a 10-man scenario</ins> where the incoming damage profile is lower and where you as a tank are responsible for more of the raid's damage proportionally to 25-man, the importance of you doing what you can to increase your output is amplified by a significant magnitude. <br/>
<br/>
<i>That being said</i>, <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> bosses hit harder than what we may be used to in this expansion thus far, and focusing on being more towards the beef side of the tankiness spectrum during progression, especially on 25-man, will not be a bad idea. <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=55308/warlord-zonozz">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Warlord Zon'ozz</span></a> will kill tanks in one global without good CD management during high stacks of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=104543/focused-anger">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_unholyfrenzy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Focused Anger</span></a>, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56427/warmaster-blackhorn">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Warmaster Blackhorn</span></a> can take you from 100-0 in one <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20243/devastate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Devastate</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=106400/impale">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_searingarrow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Impale</span></a> from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56173/deathwing">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathwing</span></a> does over 1,000,000 damage in one hit.  Once we get the 30% HP, absorb, and damage buff, however, you'll probably be able to get away with playing with any type of gear, even cloth. <br/>
<br/>
<i>
<b>TL;DR:</b> Don't neglect offensive stats, enchants, and trinkets, but don't grief your raid by being overly focused on DPS. Find a balance that works for you and your raid.</i>
