<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Blood DK Phase 4</h3>Because of the 1600 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> cap and with the raid releasing on the Thursday of the same week, you'll be able to acquire a maximum of 1 item before the raid is released. Far from everyone will be looking to maximize their power for week 1, and far from everyone is going into this raid tier with full BIS gear from the previous tier, so take this list with a grain of salt. The order will differ greatly from person to person as we don't have any of the tier 13 on the Valor vendor this time around. There are a lot of caveats as to when and if you'd like to pick up a certain Valor item; will outline it below to the best of my ability, but try to think about why you're buying a certain piece, rather than following the priority list blindly.<br/>
<br/>Remember that <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77317/heartcrusher-wristplates">
<img alt="Heartcrusher Wristplates" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_plate_raiddeathknight_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heartcrusher Wristplates</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77170/kneebreaker-boots">
